    "created_at": "2017-08-02T13:02:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-02T13:02:56Z",
    "body": "Although I don't remember how things ended up like this, it certainly looks intentional that the [reaches the end](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#reaches-the-end) steps run synchronously at step 11 of [seek](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#dom-media-seek). That could queue a task to fire timeupdate/pause/ended that will be run before the tasks to fire timeupdate/seeked at the of seek.\r\n\r\n@jwwang, does this match what you've seen browsers actually do, or do you think we have a spec problem here?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
