    "created_at": "2017-08-03T02:11:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-03T02:11:37Z",
    "body": "It is not really a spec. bug but there is some weirdness in it:\r\n1. It makes more sense to me that 'ended' should be the last event. Having 'timeupdate' (step 16) fired after 'ended' is weird to me.\r\n2. It is possible to observe (media.ended && media.seeking) for \"reaches the end of the media resource\" is not run in the same synchronous section of step 14. It is weird to say playback has ended but seeking is still going on.\r\n3. It is possible to fire 'loadeddata' after 'seeked' which might be fired after 'ended'.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
